{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## APPLY ABORTED — the plan trips AC5's STOP condition (live credentials would be DESTROYED)\n\nOperator approved retrying `terraform apply` once the templatefile bug was fixed. The fix is\nverified (guard passes, mutation-checked, change 2317 pushed), so I ran `terraform plan` from\nthe fixed tree. **`terraform plan` now RUNS TO COMPLETION** — AC1's mechanism is confirmed\nrepaired; the template no longer fails to evaluate.\n\nBut the plan itself must NOT be applied.\n\n    Plan: 6 to add, 1 to change, 4 to destroy.\n\n**The four destroys are exactly the parameters AC5 names as a hard stop:**\n\n    !! delete  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_plain_seeded[\"/rebar/prod/jira-url\"]\n    !! delete  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_plain_seeded[\"/rebar/prod/jira-user\"]\n    !! delete  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/jira-api-token\"]\n    !! delete  aws_ssm_parameter.jira_project\n\nAC5: *'the three import blocks ... must ADOPT the operator-seeded parameters. If the plan shows\nany of them DESTROYED, RECREATED, or having its value overwritten, STOP — those hold live\ncredentials.'* All three are DESTROYED, not adopted. Aborted; no apply was run.\n\n**Blast radius (AC6), stated in full.** The plan proposes far more than 'the four SSM\nparameters and the user_data in-place update':\n\n    create  aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.mcp_mem_abort\n    create  aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.mcp_retire_cap\n    create  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-claude\"]\n    create  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-codex\"]\n    create  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/mcp-client-pat-copilot\"]\n    create  aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets[\"/rebar/prod/mcp-tickets-pat\"]\n    update  aws_instance.gerrit\n\nTwo additional hazards beyond the destroys:\n\n1. **The four created `mcp-*-pat` parameters are LIVE client credentials in use right now** by\n   the Claude/Codex/Copilot MCP clients and the tickets push path. Creating them from terraform\n   would write terraform's notion of their values over the operator-seeded ones.\n2. **`update aws_instance.gerrit` is the `user_data` change, and it is NOT benign.** Modifying\n   user_data requires an EC2 stop/start — this is what caused the ~3-minute production outage on\n   the previous apply attempt, because the plan's 'in-place update' wording was read as safe.\n   Recording it here so the next reader does not repeat that inference.\n\n**Diagnosis of the destroys.** The config no longer declares the Jira parameters at the\naddresses the state holds them (`rebar_plain_seeded` / `rebar_secrets[jira-*]`), so terraform\ntreats them as removed and schedules deletion, while adding the MCP PATs under new keys. That\nis an address refactor that wants `moved`/`import` blocks, not a destroy-and-create — the\nimport blocks AC5 refers to are evidently not adopting.\n\n**AC1 is met** (`terraform plan` completes). **AC4 is NOT met and cannot be met by this plan** —\napplying it would delete live Jira credentials and overwrite live MCP PATs. The config needs\nfixing before any apply is safe. Escalated."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787905372467067001,"uuid":"b99b44a5-0771-472d-908f-6157637a884c"}